    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed lineup, as core assets like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined by an off-day, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains held out on the IL. In this thin environment, **Drake Baldwin** emerges as our strongest play with a score of 58.47. His leadoff designation against Nola provides a significant volume boost to his floor, effectively offsetting the challenge of facing a high-caliber arm. While the SP_xERA of 3.93 for Nola suggests a difficult matchup, **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s efficiency is stabilized by his consistent role at the top of the order, making him the anchor of our limited offensive output today.\n\nThe utility spot was the most contentious decision, with **Dominic Smith** ultimately securing the start with a score of 44.65. While his raw projection hovered in the marginal range, he nudged ahead of internal depth options like **Andy Pages** and **Heliot Ramos** due to a favorable platoon edge that slightly elevated his ceiling despite a bottom-third lineup placement. We continue to monitor the status of **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** for future rotation; however, for today, the focus remains entirely on navigating the volatility of Nola\u2019s repertoire. The primary risk remains the lack of high-end depth; should **Dominic Smith** struggle against the high-leverage looks Nola provides, our 5x5 category standing could slip, as we lack the elite sprint speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** or **Wade Meckler** to manufacture runs in a low-scoring game script.",
